1e:["$","div","4",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"The order of draw exists to prevent additive carryover between tubes. Drawing out of order can produce results that are wrong but entirely plausible — EDTA carryover into a chemistry tube falsely elevates potassium and falsely lowers calcium, and nothing about the result looks anomalous. A patient can be treated for a condition they do not have on the strength of a tube drawn in the wrong sequence."]}]
